-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of X₁(N)→ X₁(M) away from the cusps
-- statement:
--   Let $M,N$ be non-zero natural numbers with $4 \le M$ and $M \mid N$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Inside the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ consider two intermediate fields over $L$: $K$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField N)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!) \to L(\!(q)\!)$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField N`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $\Gamma_1(N)$; and $K'$, assumed equal to the same construction for level $M$. Assume $K' \le K$ as subfields of $L(\!(q)\!)$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the image under that coefficientwise map of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), namely $q^{-1}$ times the rational $q$-expansion series $jNumQ$. Finally let $P$ be a place of $K$ over $L$, i.e. a valuation subring of $K$ containing $L$, not all of $K$, and a principal ideal ring, and assume $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) \ge 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_P$ is the normalised additive valuation attached to $P$. Then the ramification index of $P$ along the inclusion $K' \hookrightarrow K$ — the least $n > 0$ such that $\operatorname{ord}_P(f) = n$ for some non-zero $f \in K'$ — equals $1$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the statement that, for $M \ge 4$ and $M \mid N$, the covering $X_1(N) \to X_1(M)$ is unramified at every point where $j$ is finite, the ramification of the tower being concentrated at the cusps (where $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) < 0$); it rests on the torsion-freeness of $\Gamma_1(M)$ for $M \ge 4$ together with multiplicativity of ramification indices in the tower $L(j) \subseteq K' \subseteq K$. It is reduced here to the case $L = \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and is used in the proof that the level-raising maps between the charts of $X_1$ are finite and étale, and in the construction of places with $\operatorname{ord} = 1$ on $X_1(N)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_eq_one_of_ord_nonneg_laurentBaseChange_x1FunctionField_of_dvd.lean

